Why this file is bundled
- workOrderPdf uses pdfkit. Standard fonts (Helvetica) have no CJK glyphs, so
  Chinese in the work-order PDF becomes mojibake unless a CJK font is embedded.
- This region subset covers simplified-Chinese itineraries, customer names, and
  place names (not only the fixed headings). A labels-only subset would still
  garble body text such as 呼伦贝尔 / 莫尔道嘎.
- pdfkit subsets the embedded font to the characters actually drawn, so the
  exported PDF stays small even though this source file is about 8.0 MiB.
- On-disk size fits the cloud function ZipFile API (base64 payload under 20MB).
  No cold-start download is required, so export works when outbound network
  or globalConfig.alert.pdfFontFileID / pdfFontUrl is unset.
- Those two config fields remain optional overrides. If an override is missing,
  invalid, or fails to register, generation falls back to this file.
